7] [17592186543674 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186363363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546100 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546111 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546100 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546100 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $f(x,y,z)=(-1)\\cdot (z)+(-2)\\cdot (x)+(3)\\cdot (y),$ where $x=t - 3 s$, $y=- s - t$, $z=- s + 2 t$. Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546100 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4295ba3c-10ba-5642-926e-19c46049c936" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546100 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-2,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =-3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =-1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(-2)\\cdot (-3)+(3)\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =6 - 3 + 1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546109 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546117 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546109 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546109 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $f(x,y,z)=(-3)\\cdot (x)+(3)\\cdot (y)+(3)\\cdot (z),$ where $x=s + t$, $y=- t + 2 s$, $z=- 3 s + 2 t$. Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546109 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7c95ae4a-2914-518f-a79c-f9b0d