 $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-2,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-3,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =-3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =3, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(-2)\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (3)+(-2)\\cdot (2) \\\\  & =6 - 9 - 4 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546116 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546119 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546116 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546116 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $f(x,y,z)=(-1)\\cdot (x)+(-1)\\cdot (z)+(2)\\cdot (y),$ where $x=t + 3 s$, $y=s - t$, $z=- 3 s + 2 t$. Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546116 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8e3a4bcf-977b-579b-8b15-e3ddf5401153" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546116 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(-1)\\cdot (3)+(2)\\cdot (1)+(-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-3 + 2 + 3 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546118 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546108 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546118 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546118 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $f(x,y,z)=(-1)\\cdot (y)+(2)\\cdot (x)+(3)\\cdot (z),$ where $x=t - 3 s$, $y=- t - 2 s$, $z=- s + 2 t$. Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546118 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a14e747f-884d-5e7d-bb04-a68302f8fbf5" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546118 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =-3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =-2, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(2)\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+(3)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-6 + 2 - 3 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546131 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186166750.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546131 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "31ced20f-2d73-550c-b02a-cc3a89cd99eb" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552854 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186553606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552854 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186553607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552854 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186553632 #edb/ref 175