12) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}) \\\\  & =6 (3 t + 2) ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} + (3 t - 2) (3 t + 2)^{3} + 1) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561364 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186561361 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561364 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561364 #edb/ref 1071 "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=4 t^{2}$ and $y=t^{4},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561364 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ba6447ed-c55a-5176-ab21-a18af111a0e0" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561364 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =4 t^{6} e^{4 t^{6}} + e^{4 t^{6}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =16 t^{4} e^{4 t^{6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=8 t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=4 t^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(4 t^{6} e^{4 t^{6}} + e^{4 t^{6}})\\cdot (8 t)+(16 t^{4} e^{4 t^{6}})\\cdot (4 t^{3}) \\\\  & =8 t e^{4 t^{6}} + (32 t^{7} e^{4 t^{6}}) + (64 t^{